# The launch countdown. See docs/planning/marketing-site-plan.md §9.
#
# UNSET (the default) renders NO countdown — the chip above the headline reads
# "Ontario · launching soon". Forgetting to set this therefore yields no
# countdown, never a wrong one.
#
# It deliberately does NOT fall back to a waitlist counter: a signup count is on
# the do-not-publish list until it can be read live from the database, and an
# invented number on a page whose whole claim is honesty about numbers would be
# the worst place to start.
#
# A date in the past switches to the live state rather than counting negative.
# An unparseable value is treated as unset and logs a warning outside production.
#
# RFC 3339, e.g. 2026-11-03T12:00:00-05:00
NEXT_PUBLIC_LAUNCH_AT=

# Where a waitlist signup is POSTed as JSON. UNSET means nothing is stored, and
# the form shows its error state rather than reporting a success it did not
# have. See src/lib/waitlist-store.ts.
WAITLIST_WEBHOOK_URL=
